# {{name}}

An HTTP service on [id_effect](https://github.com/Industrial/id_effect), generated by `id-effect new --template service`.

```sh
cargo test     # the router in process
{{#if pg}}
docker compose up -d db
export DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres
{{/if}}
cargo run      # http://127.0.0.1:8080/health (variables: .env.example)
```

If it does not start, `id-effect doctor` checks the toolchain, the id_effect versions, the
`.env.example` keys, `DATABASE_URL`, docker and the port (`cargo install id_effect_tool` for the
`id-effect` command). `cargo run -- --describe-layers` (or `id-effect doctor --graph`) prints the
layer graph that `src/main.rs` registers.

| Route | What |
|---|---|
| `GET /` | the greeting, counted in `greetings_total` |
| `GET /hello/{name}` | a typed route: `{name}` (1 to 32 characters) is decoded through a schema; anything else is a `422` Problem+JSON |
| `GET /health` | liveness: `200` while the process runs |
| `GET /ready` | readiness: the `HealthRegistry` checks as JSON, `503` when one is down or once shutdown has started |
| `GET /metrics` | Prometheus text: `http_server_requests_total` by method, route and status, runtime gauges; only for a scrape sending `Authorization: Bearer $METRICS_TOKEN` (unset: `401` to everyone) |

Deny by default: every route declares who may call it. The typed routes say `.public()` or `.guard(..)`; the plain Axum routes (`/health`, `/ready`, `/metrics`) are declared in `plain_routes()`. `app()` applies the deny-by-default layer (`AccessLayer`) after the last route, so a route added without a declaration answers `404`; add it as a typed route or to `plain_routes()`.

Every request passes through `SecurityLayer::recommended`: CSRF tokens on state-changing requests, a nonce-based CSP, HSTS / `X-Frame-Options` / `nosniff` headers and signed cookies (`COOKIE_KEY`). The middleware stack also gives each request an `x-request-id` (and a span), compresses responses, answers a request running past `REQUEST_TIMEOUT` with `503` and a body over `BODY_LIMIT` with `413`; rejections are RFC 9457 Problem+JSON (`application/problem+json`).

## Security posture

`main.rs` runs the posture check of ADR 0013 before it serves and prints the report: console guarded, docs closed, mesh transport encrypted, redaction policy non-empty, SSRF guard on, CSRF on, load shedding on, no memory-only security state, no unaccepted opt-out. `ID_EFFECT_PROFILE` picks the profile (`dev` by default; `config/deploy.yml` sets `prod`). Under `prod` a failed probe stops the service. Every weakening of a default is a named `dangerous_*` / `insecure_*` call that records itself; to run one in `prod`, accept it with a reason in `config/prod.toml`:

```toml
[security.accepted_risks]
"id_effect_axum::HostConfig::dangerous_no_load_shedding" = "the proxy caps concurrency; reviewed 2026-10"
```

`posture()` in `src/lib.rs` states what `app()` serves; keep it true when you change the app. `tests/http.rs` checks that the generated app passes the `prod` check (`template_service_passes_prod_posture`).
{{#if console}}

In the `prod` profile the console answers `401` to every request until you put real authentication (`id_effect_kit::auth`) in front of its guard: the local-operator shortcut exists only in `dev`.
{{/if}}

## Layout

- `src/lib.rs` — `app()`: the router, testable without a socket; `plain_routes()`: the access of its plain routes; `posture()`: what it states for the posture check; `serve()`: serves it, counting in-flight requests for the drain.
- `src/main.rs` — loads `HOST`, `PORT`, `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_SECS`, `MAX_IN_FLIGHT` and `COOKIE_KEY`, runs the posture check, serves until SIGINT / SIGTERM, then drains in-flight requests (for up to `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_SECS`) while `/ready` answers `503` and new connections are still accepted.
{{#if pg}}
- `src/db.rs` — the PostgreSQL pool (`DATABASE_URL`), the migrations in `migrations/` applied on start (`id_effect_kit::sql::migrate::run`: tracked in `_id_effect_migrations`, one transaction each, an advisory lock across replicas), the `db` check behind `/ready`.
- `migrations/` — `0001_init.sql`; add the next with `id-effect migrate new <name>`, apply with `id-effect migrate run` (or start the service), and never edit one that ran (`id-effect migrate check` fails on a changed or pending migration).
{{/if}}
{{#if jobs}}
{{#if !pg}}
- `src/jobs/` — background jobs (`id_effect_kit::jobs`): `registry()` and the `worker()` that `main.rs` runs in the same process; the queue is in memory (lost on restart; `--db pg` makes it the `id_effect_jobs` table). `id-effect generate job <name>` adds a job.
{{/if}}
{{#if pg}}
- `src/jobs/` — background jobs (`id_effect_kit::jobs`): `registry()`, the `worker()` that `main.rs` runs in the same process, and the queue, the `id_effect_jobs` table created on start. `id-effect generate job <name>` adds a job.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if console}}
- `src/console.rs` — the operator console (`id_effect_kit::console`) on `127.0.0.1:CONSOLE_PORT` (default 9090): `/_console` (dashboard) and `/_console/api/*`, behind a guard requiring the `operator` role. In `dev` every request on the loopback listener has it; in any other profile nobody does, so the console answers `401` until real authentication is in front of the guard. It answers only to its own host: a `Host` or `Origin` outside `CONSOLE_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (default: the bind address) is answered `403`.
{{/if}}
- `tests/http.rs` — the routes, the security headers, readiness and metrics.
- `tests/shutdown.rs` — SIGTERM: `/ready` turns `503` while an in-flight request completes.

## Run it elsewhere

- `docker compose up --build` — the image from `Dockerfile` and the services it needs.
- `config/deploy.yml` — a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org) config: set the image, servers and registry, then `kamal setup`.
{{#if pg}}
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — fmt, clippy, test and a docker build on every push, and a job that applies `migrations/` to a PostgreSQL service with `id-effect migrate run` and gates on `id-effect migrate check` (it installs `id_effect_tool`).
{{/if}}
{{#if !pg}}
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — fmt, clippy, test and a docker build on every push.
{{/if}}

## Batteries

`Cargo.toml` enables the `id_effect_kit` features [{{kit_features}}]. `id-effect new --template service --db pg` wires the `sql-pg` and `migrate` features (PostgreSQL client, versioned migrations, `db` readiness check); `--otel` the `otel` feature (OTLP export of traces, metrics and logs, configured by the `OTEL_*` variables, request spans included; with `--db pg`, `Database::sql()` is the SQL capability with a `db.query` span per statement); `--jobs` the `jobs` feature (`src/jobs/` and an in-process worker); `--console` the `console` feature (the operator console on a loopback port).
